                        "form": "августе́йших"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7f13f57f-022c-3784-a6cc-602896b1b63d",
                        "entry_id": "ffcb5149-574c-3dc8-96bc-c8afa198ca3a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "являющийся членом императорской семьи"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "52f7ee1c-8f7c-462b-a6a5-e7eed8ebd4dc",
                                "sense_id": "7f13f57f-022c-3784-a6cc-602896b1b63d",
                                "text": "— Они оба в гостях в Дании, с ними же и августейшая мать государя, Мария Фёдоровна."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f72a6097-8d9a-41ee-9934-cd0f9cb7a625",
                                "sense_id": "7f13f57f-022c-3784-a6cc-602896b1b63d",
                                "text": "В 1759 году он отозван был в своё отечество, а в 29 день июня последовавшего года императрица благоволила вверить ему надзирание над воспитанием великого князя Павла Петровича, важную должность, которую он беспрерывно исправлял до самого бракосочетания августейшего его питомца."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c88214aa-51bf-4d1d-a068-deab163e9e24",
                                "sense_id": "7f13f57f-022c-3784-a6cc-602896b1b63d",
                                "text": "Здесь же в первый раз Арефа услыхал, что проявился в казаках не прост человек, прозвищем Пугач, и что этот человек принял на себя августейшую персону государя Петра III."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "657a47f2-986d-47c9-94d8-91dbe15fc3dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "ffcb5149-574c-3dc8-96bc-c8afa198ca3a",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f13f57f-022c-3784-a6cc-602896b1b63d",
                        "target_lang_word": "august",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "august",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                        "entry_id": "a34ca746-1c7b-342f-b893-4a1a22559640",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Awe-inspiring, majestic, noble, venerable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29f1e37f-96ad-4476-a8ee-308969d17a5d",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "an august patron of the arts"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6e1119a-bc05-4446-8365-422171a0ad39",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "In the book of Pſalms there are many things ſaid of David, which ſeem capable of a much auguſter ſenſe than can be pretended to be anſwered by any thing that befel himſelf."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d188ec93-3526-408b-8199-783547c00923",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "[W]e shall not, I think, be able to find language which can convey in few words more fully the idea we should always have impressed on our minds of the august character of our Lord, than the expression, \"the word of life.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3e71627-5d63-4466-8b95-3bb0aadcfece",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "The commands of the august sovereign are the imperial commands, or the phœnix (the incomparable) mandate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b77cc4f5-c520-4c99-a6b6-1ca4d2ab0d97",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "—Inconsciously to the augustest end / Thou hast arisen: second not in rank / So much as time, to him who first ordained / That Florence, thou art to destroy, should be— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92e8e59e-23e5-4c0f-957b-0a2a4df46a99",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "The foolish dog […] flew at the cat, who in her fright and consternation took refuge behind the screen of the breakfast-room where his Majesty then was. The Mikado was greatly shocked and agitated. He took the cat into his august bosom, and summoning the chamberlain Tadataka, gave orders that Okinamaro should have a good thrashing and be banished to Dog Island at once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb966e2b-d02f-4143-adc7-391475b4f86e",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "For once the story was not about Jamie Vardy, unable to equal Jimmy Dunne's top-flight record of scoring in a dozen consecutive games, but about his august deputy Riyad Mahrez."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b779e307-641d-4fb0-a42b-165ec8269a48",
                                                "sense_id": "1692fbe6-4e97-33b5-b96f-53bc74a815d1",
                                                "text": "Countless proposals flooded in, sent by sources as august as the World Academy of Sciences and as humble as elementary schools."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a55a7a09-a1ed-3a9a-9dc3-04edcaca29e3",
                                        "entry_id": "a34ca746-1c7b-342f-b893-4a1a22559640",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of noble birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a2c4b6d-7aac-4d95-822a-f539f9daccc2",
                                                "sense_id": "a55a7a09-a1ed-3a9a-9dc3-04edcaca29e3",
                                                "text": "an august lineage"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cd09365-7534-49f2-b8b2-093961c0abe1",
                                                "sense_id": "a55a7a09-a1ed-3a9a-9dc3-04edcaca29e3",
                                                "text": "A branch of the house of Lorraine, in comparison with which even the royal race of Capet was mean, the Guises traced back their august lineage through a long line of warrior princes to the Imperial figure of Charlemagne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "august",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c8c2c80-ec5d-3385-81da-2c1d561c5325",
                                        "entry_id": "495500d2-39bf-3434-99f6-a5608dfae1f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make ripe; ripen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49df14e5-3741-3569-a21c-045ff56adebe",
                                        "entry_id": "495500d2-39bf-3434-99f6-a5608dfae1f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring to realization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "458a05fd-9000-4bd4-b6cf-84dfdf5f105c",
                                                "sense_id": "49df14e5-3741-3569-a21c-045ff56adebe",
                                                "text": "By divine science and cœlestial art / He for the cause of the dear nations toiled, / And augusted man's heavenly hopes that so, / […] / he might, by awful rites / […] / Adhæsion with Divinity achieve."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
